Introduction
Service sector includes all those economic activities
which are required for uninterrupted production
and exchange of goods. It includes specialised
services required for removing various hindrances
of trade. We know, it is very important that goods
are produced in time. However, at the same time, it
is also important that such goods reach the
consumers at the right time. Service sector helps to
achieve these twin goals.
Trade and industry is not possible without the
various service sectors liker banking, insurance,
communication, transportation, warehousing, etc.
In short, service sector is the backbone of every
business and Industry.
