☑Intangible: Services are intangible, i.e., these cannot be seen or
touched. We cannot find out the quality of service before taking
it. One can find out the quality only after experiencing it. So,
supplier must try to offer good quality services to customers so
that they demand them again after experiencing them.
Lack of Homogeneity or Inconsistency: Services have to be
performed each time according to the demands and expectation
of each customer. Same services may be provided differently by
different service providers. For example, the banking services
provided by nationalised banks are quite different from the
banking services provided by private sector or foreign banks.
