Inventory (loss): The main feature of services is that services
are consumed at the same time, when they are produced. So,
there is no need to maintain inventory or stock of services If
service is not consumed immediately then it is a total loss.
Non-transferability or Inseparability: The services cannot be
separated from the provider of services. These are produced
and consumed at the same place only. For example, we
cannot separate the medical service provided by a doctor
from the doctor. Doctor and his services are inseparable.
Similarly, it applies to lawyer, a chartered accountant, etc.
Customer's Participation or Involvement: To experience a
service the participation of the customer is essential. For
example, telephone companies provide telephone services but
to use this service customer has to make or receive the call.
